{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy gives clear states a forward-biased action, sends any obstacle observation into a dedicated recovery state, uses backward motion only for front-obstacle escape, uses directed turns for side obstacles, and returns to forward exploration immediately on path_clear. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted by non-critical clear readings, while obstacle events can still redirect to safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant sensing from motion capability so specifications can bind sensor outcomes to exactly one safe controllable action per policy state.",
    "Use one exploration spec plus one front-recovery spec, one left-recovery spec, one right-recovery spec, and one rare last-resort scan spec to keep recovery conservative but coverage-oriented."
  ],
